{"id":"1a1de26f-149f-4067-b5f2-5c758f8dd4e5","object":"chat.completion","created":1784885031,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    edges = case['edges']\\n    refinement = case['refinement']\\n    from collections import defaultdict\\n    agg = defaultdict(float)\\n    for u, v, w in edges:\\n        cu = refinement[u]\\n        cv = refinement[v]\\n        if cu == cv:\\n            key = (cu, cv)\\n        else:\\n            key = tuple(sorted([cu, cv]))\\n        agg[key] += w\\n    aggregate_edges = sorted([[c1, c2, w] for (c1, c2), w in agg.items()])\\n    members = defaultdict(list)\\n    for v, c in refinement.items():\\n        members[c].append(v)\\n    for c in members:\\n        members[c].sort()\\n    members_dict = {c: members[c] for c in sorted(members.keys())}\\n    return {\\\"aggregate_edges\\\": aggregate_edges, \\\"members\\\": members_dict}\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) as per the output schema. The task is DATA-LEI-02. The case payload has edges and refinement. The refinement maps vertices to groups (communities). We need to produce:\n\n- \"aggregate_edges\": an array of arrays, each with 3 elements: [string, string, number]. It represents edges between refined communities, with summed weights. Undirected, so should canonicalize order of the two community names (e.g., sorted alphabetical). Also include self-loops (when both endpoints map to same community). Sum weights for each pair.\n\n- \"members\": an object with dynamic keys from \"case.refinement.values()\". That means the keys are the values in the refinement mapping (the community names). For each community name, the value is an array of strings: the original vertex names that map to that community. The schema says \"dynamicKeysFrom\": \"case.refinement.values()\", so the keys of the members object must exactly be the set of values from refinement. They mus